  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1429\">\n<li data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1217\">\n<p data-start=\"1119\" data-end=\"1217\"><strong data-start=\"1119\" data-end=\"1132\">Positive:</strong> Suggestive of celiac disease; especially relevant in patients with IgA deficiency.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1332\">\n<p data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1332\"><strong data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1233\">Negative:</strong> Unlikely to have active celiac disease, but consider total IgA level to rule out IgA deficiency.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1429\">\n<p data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1429\"><strong data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1350\">Borderline:</strong> May require repeat testing or further evaluation (e.g., biopsy, HLA typing).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1429\">\n<p data-start=\"1335\" data-end=\"1429\">Anti-tTG IgG testing is useful in patients who are&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1484\" data-end=\"1501\">IgA deficient</strong> or have inconclusive Anti-tTG IgA results.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
